WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.799 --> 00:00:05.480
If you're anything like us, you had a neatly-organized
laundry list of films to catch last year.

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:09.880
But with all that focus on big-ticket films
- like Star Wars: The Last Jedi, Wonder Woman,

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:14.130
and Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2 - a ton
of amazing picks have slipped under the radar.

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:17.189
We're here to show you the best of the bunch.

00:00:17.189 --> 00:00:18.189
The Big Sick

00:00:18.189 --> 00:00:23.109
Based on the true story of how Pakistan-born
aspiring comedian Kumail Nanjiani met his

00:00:23.109 --> 00:00:27.460
wife, Emily V. Gordon, The Big Sick is a prime
example of a midsummer sleeper hit.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.460
"She's white."

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:29.550
"A white girl?

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:32.530
You can look like you and date a white girl"

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:34.280
"It's okay… we hate terrorists."

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:39.210
The Big Sick rejects sappy sentimentality
in favor of organic dialogue, irresistible

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:43.780
sincerity, and a sharp sense of humor -- even
when Emily is struck down with a mysterious

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:46.660
illness that Nanjiani navigates with her parents.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:50.660
Nanjiani and Zoe Kazan offer up two of the
year's best performances.

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:55.749
Hilarious and refreshingly honest, with bawdy
jokes and an undeniable emotional intelligence,

00:00:55.749 --> 00:00:58.980
The Big Sick is a little film with a great
big heart.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:00.179
A Ghost Story

00:01:00.179 --> 00:01:04.159
You may have missed this unique drama, but
you'll surely recognize Academy Award winner

00:01:04.159 --> 00:01:08.470
Casey Affleck and Academy Award-nominated
Rooney Mara as a husband and wife that have

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:09.900
been separated by death.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:14.580
Affleck plays a struggling musician turned
white-sheeted ghost straight out of, well,

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:15.640
a ghost story.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:19.980
As he slips away, Affleck works to unlock
questions of his past, along with the enigma

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.180
of existence.

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:25.530
Directed by David Lowery, the film is bursting
with fantasy, creating an experience that

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:28.840
lingers on the pangs of love and the hope
hidden in grief.

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:30.000
The Survivalist

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.930
Directed by Stephen Fingleton, The Survivalist
imagines a post-apocalyptic wilderness where

00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:40.610
Irish actor Martin McCann protects his makeshift
farm from invaders with shotguns and traps.

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:44.410
When an ailing woman offers her beautiful
teenage daughter in exchange for shelter,

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:46.140
he mistakenly lets his guard down.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:51.360
Ravaged by lust, he turns his back on his
code—and opens up a world of untold danger.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:56.240
The Survivalist debuted at Tribeca in 2015,
but didn't screen in America until May of

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:57.420
2017.

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:01.980
Its high contrast color palette, fast pace,
and thought-provoking plot have earned critical

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:02.980
acclaim.

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:05.910
Be prepared to watch this one from the edge
of your seat.

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:06.910
Mindhorn

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:11.030
Produced by Ridley Scott and directed by Sean
Foley, this British indie centers on make-believe

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:16.000
actor Richard Thorncroft who tasted fame as
Mindhorn, an 80's TV detective.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:18.630
Three decades later, he's a shadow of his
former self.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:23.140
With no acting work to keep him busy, the
self-involved egomaniac has to track down

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:27.030
a Mindhorn-obsessed murderer who will only
fess up to the fictional character.

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:32.140
Goofy gags, high-profile cameos, and cheeky
one-liners push Mindhorn into "instant gem"

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:33.140
territory.

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:34.580
"We're all gonna die.

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:35.300
Get over it.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.220
Some with a bang.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:37.160
Some with a whimper.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:38.720
Some with a weird, wasting disease."

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:40.540
Paint It Black

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:45.620
Lauded for its visual beauty, complex narrative
and solid performances, actress Amber Tamblyn's

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:50.690
directorial debut Paint It Black got a low-profile
release during its theatrical run.

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:56.470
The film follows the destructive rivalry of
Alia Shawkat's Josie and Janet McTeer's Meredith.

00:02:56.470 --> 00:03:00.470
After the death of her boyfriend Michael,
Josie attempts to piece together the circumstances

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:01.470
of his death.

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:04.970
The process forces her closer to his mother,
the menacing Meredith.

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:09.319
It's simply the only way to learn the truth—however
nightmarish it might be.

00:03:09.319 --> 00:03:10.319
Good Time

00:03:10.319 --> 00:03:13.900
Robert Pattinson has come a long way from
his glittering vampire days.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:18.310
Never has this been more evident than in Good
Time, a gritty and gorgeous crime drama directed

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:20.720
by sibling duo Josh and Benny Safdie.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:25.900
Pattinson plays Constantine aka "Connie",
who robs a bank with his developmentally disabled

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:26.980
brother Nick.

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:30.730
When Nick gets caught, Connie races against
the clock--and through the city's dangerous

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:34.240
underbelly--in a desperate attempt to free
his brother from prison.

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:39.319
With its contradictory title, Good Time has
swept up acclaim and industry accolades, including

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:42.540
a nomination for the Cannes Film Festival's
Palme d'Or

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:43.849
Logan Lucky

00:03:43.849 --> 00:03:49.040
In Steven Soderbergh's high-octane heist comedy
Logan Lucky, Channing Tatum stars as an average,

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:50.760
blue-collar joe who lost everything.

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:55.709
"I was let go, for liability reasons, involving
insurance."

00:03:55.709 --> 00:04:00.100
He recruits his one-armed brother, played
by Adam Driver, and a number of other zany

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:02.709
characters to rob a major NASCAR speedway.

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:07.209
Featuring an explosive made of gummy bears,
a heartfelt rendition of "Take Me Home, Country

00:04:07.209 --> 00:04:11.850
Roads," and stellar performances from A-list
actors, it's hard to believe Logan Lucky flew

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:12.850
under anyone's radar.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:16.549
But that's all the more reason to see it as
soon as possible.

00:04:16.549 --> 00:04:17.549
Lucky

00:04:17.549 --> 00:04:21.749
This film about an independent 90-year-old
atheist shines with complexity and emotional

00:04:21.749 --> 00:04:24.400
weight that resonate both on and off screen.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:29.740
In his final film, the late Harry Dean Stanton
stars as Lucky, a retired World War II veteran

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:32.180
in search of enlightenment at the end of his
life.

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:36.569
The warmly lit Arizona landscape and deeply
engrossing narrative make you wish you hadn't

00:04:36.569 --> 00:04:41.800
missed Stanton's glorious swan song — but
feel lucky to have seen it once you finally

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:42.919
do.

00:04:42.919 --> 00:04:43.919
Super Dark Times

00:04:43.919 --> 00:04:47.689
This is a case where a film's title perfectly
describes its events.

00:04:47.689 --> 00:04:51.490
Super Dark Times is a visceral thriller about
two teenage best friends growing up in the

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:53.169
suburbs in the '90s.

00:04:53.169 --> 00:04:57.599
Their lives center around comic books, bike
rides to the corner store, Friday night hangouts,

00:04:57.599 --> 00:05:00.430
first romances, and the quest for high school
popularity.

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:05.550
But when a truly unthinkable incident occurs,
the boys lose their innocence--and each other.

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:10.080
As they navigate the murky waters of the tragedy
and its aftermath, Super Dark Times rides

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:14.479
the fine line between boyhood and manhood,
good and evil, horror and valor, spilling

00:05:14.479 --> 00:05:19.729
out onto the silver screen in waves of slow-burning
terror that will grip you by the throat.

00:05:19.729 --> 00:05:22.099
Three Billboards Outside Ebbing, Missouri

00:05:22.099 --> 00:05:26.949
Academy Award-winning director Martin McDonagh's
Three Billboards Outside Ebbing, Missouri

00:05:26.949 --> 00:05:31.659
stars Frances McDormand as a single mother
determined to seek justice for her daughter,

00:05:31.659 --> 00:05:33.150
who was violently murdered.

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:37.180
The local police department's failure to make
headway in the case pushes McDormand to rent

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:40.979
three abandoned billboards and paint each
of them with bold messages directed at the

00:05:40.979 --> 00:05:43.599
chief of police, played by Woody Harrelson.

00:05:43.599 --> 00:05:48.039
As she clashes with the townspeople in increasingly
turbulent showdowns, the quick-to-violence

00:05:48.039 --> 00:05:52.729
Officer Dixon, played by Sam Rockwell, enters
the picture, sending shockwaves through the

00:05:52.729 --> 00:05:53.729
town.

00:05:53.729 --> 00:05:59.319
With exceptional performances, Three Billboards
is harrowing, humorous, and completely unforgettable.

00:05:59.319 --> 00:06:00.449
Sylvio

00:06:00.449 --> 00:06:02.180
Sylvio isn't your average comedy.

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:07.090
Kentucker Audley and Albert Birney's joint
effort follows Sylvio Bernardi as he copes

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:08.779
with newfound small-town fame.

00:06:08.779 --> 00:06:10.750
Oh yeah, and he's also a gorilla.

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:13.689
This endearing indie will surprise you with
its authenticity.

00:06:13.689 --> 00:06:17.869
The eponymous ape's life is turned around
when, after appearing on a television show,

00:06:17.869 --> 00:06:21.300
he's mistaken for a performer and turned into
an overnight sensation.

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:26.310
However, with reputation comes repercussions,
and the gentle primate has to reconsider everything

00:06:26.310 --> 00:06:30.360
he knows about himself–and what kind of
influence the people in his life truly have

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:31.389
on him.

00:06:31.389 --> 00:06:33.289
Brawl in Cell Block 99

00:06:33.289 --> 00:06:37.669
You'd never expect to see actor Vince Vaughn
bald and covered in blood and tattoos, but

00:06:37.669 --> 00:06:41.589
that's exactly what S. Craig Zahler gives
you with his thriller, Brawl in Cell Block

00:06:41.589 --> 00:06:42.599
99.

00:06:42.599 --> 00:06:47.159
Vaughn plays Bradley Thomas, a former boxer
and recovering alcoholic who returns to dealing

00:06:47.159 --> 00:06:49.069
drugs after losing his job.

00:06:49.069 --> 00:06:53.199
Things start looking up, but then a violent
drug pickup lands Thomas with a ten-year prison

00:06:53.199 --> 00:06:54.199
sentence.

00:06:54.199 --> 00:06:58.630
Gone are his days spent with his loving wife;
he now must face cell block 99, a place where

00:06:58.630 --> 00:07:00.039
savagery reigns supreme.

00:07:00.039 --> 00:07:03.319
While this thriller saw only a limited release,
critics are calling it

00:07:03.319 --> 00:07:06.629
"A perfect example of a down-and-dirty exploitation
flick..."

00:07:06.629 --> 00:07:09.580
...and perhaps Vaughn's very best work to
date.

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:10.580
Thelma

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:14.089
This unnerving Hitchcockian thriller slowly
builds to bursting.

00:07:14.089 --> 00:07:19.029
Directed by Norwegian filmmaker Joachim Trier,
Thelma stars Eili Harboe as a young woman

00:07:19.029 --> 00:07:23.379
who waves goodbye to her religious family
and moves to the bustling city of Oslo for

00:07:23.379 --> 00:07:24.379
university.

00:07:24.379 --> 00:07:29.199
As Thelma discovers new things about herself,
she also starts suffering from violent seizures

00:07:29.199 --> 00:07:33.509
that seem to become more aggressive as her
feelings toward Anja, a beautiful student,

00:07:33.509 --> 00:07:34.550
grow stronger.

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:39.219
As it turns out, Thelma has supernatural powers,
which force her to face the darkness of her

00:07:39.219 --> 00:07:40.219
past.

00:07:40.219 --> 00:07:44.050
Don't let the foreign language aspect of Thelma
turn you away; the bone-chilling scares and

00:07:44.050 --> 00:07:46.809
shocking twists are universally understood.

00:07:46.809 --> 00:07:48.139
Thanks for watching!

00:07:48.139 --> 00:07:50.849
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:50.849 --> 00:07:52.939
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

